        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "H.1.5.3 Advantages of cross certification",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                896,
                562,
                923
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    137.0,
                    896.0
                ],
                [
                    562.0,
                    896.0
                ],
                [
                    562.0,
                    923.0
                ],
                [
                    137.0,
                    923.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The advantage of cross-certification is that it allows reduction of trust anchors needed in the entities that need to validate the certificate chains of other entities. For example:",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                946,
                1120,
                999
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    946.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    946.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    999.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    999.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "– an EV holding only one V2G root CA certificate could essentially charge at any EVSE regardless of the V2G root CA used for the generation of SECC's leaf if the V2G root CA (or any SubCA) of the SECC certificate is cross-signed by the V2G root CA certificate held by the EVCC;",
            "block_bbox": [
                208,
                1020,
                1122,
                1100
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    208.0,
                    1020.0
                ],
                [
                    1122.0,
                    1020.0
                ],
                [
                    1122.0,
                    1100.0
                ],
                [
                    208.0,
                    1100.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "– an EVSE holding only V2G root CA certificates could accept any EVs regardless of the OEM root CA certificates used for the generation of the EV's vehicle certificate if the EV's vehicle certificate is cross-signed by a V2G root CA whose V2G root CA certificate is held by the SECC.",
            "block_bbox": [
                207,
                1122,
                1122,
                1202
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    207.0,
                    1122.0
                ],
                [
                    1122.0,
